   "text": {
    "L1": "The poem follows a bird as its idea of the world grows.",
    "L2": "First, inside its eggshell, the bird thinks the world is small, round and pale blue.",
    "L3": "Next, in a straw nest beside its mother, it thinks the world is made of straw.",
    "L4": "Then it flies out and sees leaves. It says it has been very blind.",
    "L5": "Very blind means it had not understood how much it had not seen, not that its eyes were weak.",
    "L6": "At the end, the bird knows the world is too big for anyone to know fully.",
    "L7": "The poem also reaches people: as a child grows and sees more, their idea of the world grows too.",
    "L8": "In the first stanza, well and shell rhyme, so the pattern is ABCB."
   },
